`benchmark.meta description: Keeps about 15 MB of strings live while making about 1 GB of short-lived strings, then idles in the event loop for one second so the memory profile records how much the collector keeps for a small live set.
`benchmark.meta timing: not-recommended
`benchmark.meta profiles: memory,gc-runtime

/time/duration

. keep [String]
for index in 0 .. < 50000
    keep += "kept item $index with some padding text to make it longer than a word"
. checksum = 0 as Size
for round in 0 .. < 3000
    . junk [String]
    for index in 0 .. < 1000
        junk += "garbage $round $index padding padding padding padding padding"
    checksum += junk[round % junk.length].length
1s.wait()
checksum += keep.length
-- "bench-result allocation/churn-small-live checksum=$checksum"
